                "Welcome to the Grand Master Capstone of Banking, Treasury & Credit Operations. Over the past sixty intensive days, you have systematically explored and engineered every operational, quantitative, regulatory, and technological layer that constitutes the modern enterprise banking system. You began in Month 1 with the foundational mechanics of fractional reserve banking, customer deposit mobilization, working capital appraisal, and credit monitoring. You then ascended in Month 2 to the highest echelons of institutional banking: forensic asset classification under statutory IRAC norms, Asset-Liability Management (ALM) duration matching, Basel III regulatory capital ratios, OTC derivatives and interest rate swap hedging, central banking monetary operations, sovereign debt primary dealing, Open Banking API architecture, and ESG climate risk stress testing.",
                "To command this sprawling financial machinery at the executive level, you must synthesize these disparate disciplines into a single, cohesive mental and operational model: 'The Unified Enterprise Balance Sheet'. A commercial bank is not merely a collection of isolated business units—retail branches, corporate lending desks, treasury trading rooms, and digital product teams; it is a highly leveraged, dynamic financial organism where every transaction on the asset side reverberates across liabilities, liquidity buffers, and regulatory capital reserves. When a loan officer sanctions a ₹100 crore corporate facility, they simultaneously consume regulatory capital, expand risk-weighted assets (RWA), create future liquidity funding requirements, alter the structural interest rate duration of the banking book, and introduce credit and climate risk exposures.",
